# Plan: Implement PWM Functions Using Existing ESP32-S3 LEDC Driver

## Context

The file `packages/demos/esp_test/esp_test_main.c` has stub PWM lower-half functions that don't actually control hardware. The user wants working PWM output. Since ESP32-S3 already has a complete LEDC PWM lower-half driver (`esp32s3_ledc.c`), the simplest correct approach is to use it directly rather than reimplementing hardware access.

## File to Modify

- `packages/demos/esp_test/esp_test_main.c`

## Changes

### 1. Add ESP32-S3 LEDC header include

```c
#include "esp32s3_ledc.h"
```

This provides `esp32s3_ledc_init(int timer)` which returns a fully configured `pwm_lowerhalf_s*`.

### 2. Simplify `my_pwm_init()`

Replace the manual struct setup and stub ops with:

```c
int my_pwm_init(void)
{
    struct pwm_lowerhalf_s *pwm;

    pwm = esp32s3_ledc_init(0);  /* Use LEDC timer 0 */
    if (!pwm)
    {
        printf("Failed to init LEDC PWM\n");
        return -ENODEV;
    }

    int ret = pwm_register("/dev/pwm0", pwm);
    if (ret < 0)
    {
        printf("Failed to register PWM: %d\n", ret);
        return ret;
    }

    printf("PWM device registered successfully\n");
    return OK;
}
```

### 3. Remove unused code

- Remove `my_pwm_priv_s` struct (not needed — the LEDC driver has its own private data)
- Remove `my_pwm_setup`, `my_pwm_shutdown`, `my_pwm_start`, `my_pwm_stop`, `my_pwm_ioctl` stubs
- Remove `g_my_pwm_ops` and `g_my_pwm_dev`

### 4. Fix `main()` — remove infinite loop

The `while(1){}` blocks forever. Replace with a timed loop:

```c
int main(int argc, FAR char *argv[])
{
    int fd;
    struct pwm_info_s info;

    my_pwm_init();

    fd = open("/dev/pwm0", O_RDWR);
    if (fd < 0)
    {
        printf("Failed to open PWM device\n");
        return -1;
    }

    printf("PWM opened\n");

    info.frequency = 1000;  /* 1kHz */
    info.duty = 32768;      /* 50% duty (16-bit: 32768/65536) */

    if (ioctl(fd, PWMIOC_SETCHARACTERISTICS, (unsigned long)&info) < 0)
    {
        printf("Failed to set PWM characteristics\n");
        close(fd);
        return -1;
    }

    if (ioctl(fd, PWMIOC_START, 0) < 0)
    {
        printf("Failed to start PWM\n");
        close(fd);
        return -1;
    }

    printf("PWM running at %dHz, 50%% duty\n", info.frequency);
    sleep(10);  /* Run for 10 seconds */

    ioctl(fd, PWMIOC_STOP, 0);
    close(fd);
    printf("PWM stopped\n");

    return OK;
}
```

### 5. Clean up duplicate includes

The file has duplicate `#include` lines. Remove duplicates.

